## Architectural Layers (Hexagonal Architecture)

All application code resides under `src/{{ package_name }}/`:

```
src/{{ package_name }}/
├── application/       # Pure domain logic, use cases & orchestration (Singular naming)
│   ├── model/         # Immutable entities and value objects (using @dataclass(slots=True, frozen=True))
│   │   └── user.py
│   ├── port/          # Protocol interfaces (typing.Protocol)
│   │   └── user_repository.py
│   └── service/       # Application services orchestrating CQRS workflows
│       └── user_service.py
├── infrastructure/    # Concrete adapters implementing application ports
│   └── adapter/
│       └── in_memory_user_repository.py
├── presentation/      # Delivery mechanisms and composition root
│   └── cli/
│       └── app.py
├── shared/            # Cross-cutting fail-closed primitives
│   └── exception/
│       └── errors.py
└── main.py            # Entry point calling presentation CLI
```

### Dependency Inversion Rule
- Dependencies flow **inward only**:
  `presentation` / `infrastructure` -> `application`.
- The `application` layer must **never** import from `infrastructure` or `presentation`, nor from external I/O libraries (databases, HTTP clients, UI frameworks).
- Decouple all external systems using `typing.Protocol` interfaces defined in `application/port/`.

