## Testing & Quality Discipline

### 1. Behavioral TDD (Red-Green-Refactor)
- Write the failing behavioral test first.
- Implement the minimal viable code to turn the test green.
- Refactor for cleanliness and modularity while keeping tests passing.

### 2. Vanilla Pytest BDD Format
All tests must structure behavior explicitly using Given/When/Then:

```python
def test_create_user_service() -> None:
    """Verify that creating a user successfully persists and returns the entity."""
    # Given: an empty repository and an active user service
    repo = InMemoryUserRepository()
    service = UserService(repository=repo)

    # When: the user creation command is handled
    user = service.create_user(user_id="u-1", email="alice@example.com", name="Alice")

    # Then: the user is persisted and returned with expected attributes
    assert user.id == "u-1"
    assert user.name == "Alice"
    assert repo.get_by_id("u-1") == user
```

### 3. Verification Commands
Always verify changes locally using `just`:
```bash
# Install agent skills
just setup-skills

# Run all unit and integration tests
just test

# Check formatting and linting
just lint

# Format code automatically
just format

# Full validation (lint + test)
just check
```

